From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: W4HO <87742609+W4HO-ham@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 13:53:22 -0647
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: mfd: samsung,s2mpg14-pmic: Add the interrupt
 line

The S2MPG14 reports its PMIC events in-band, and the Tensor G4's VGPIO2AP
block raises them as one level interrupt that stays pending until written
back, the same arrangement the S2MPG12 binding describes. Add the
interrupt, the phandle to the VGPIO2AP system registers and
wakeup-source, and say how the interrupt reaches the host.

Unlike on the S2MPG12, the interrupt stays optional. The PMIC's rails
(the touchscreen and eUSB2 supplies) work without it, and the Pixel 9a
and Pixel 8 Pro device trees describe the PMIC without one; a board that
leaves it out only loses the PMIC's events, the RTC alarm among them.
The interrupt can't be acknowledged without the sysreg, so it depends on
the phandle, and wakeup-source, which means nothing without the
interrupt, depends on the interrupt.

Signed-off-by: W4HO <87742609+W4HO-ham@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 .../bindings/mfd/samsung,s2mpg14-pmic.yaml    | 27 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 27 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/mfd/samsung,s2mpg14-pmic.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/mfd/samsung,s2mpg14-pmic.yaml
index 5a94a6545..38b4b835d 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/mfd/samsung,s2mpg14-pmic.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/mfd/samsung,s2mpg14-pmic.yaml
@@ -14,10 +14,27 @@ description: |
   Its LDO4M and LDO25M outputs supply the analog and digital touchscreen
   power rails.
 
+  It has no interrupt line of its own: it reports events in-band, and the
+  SoC's VGPIO2AP system registers turn them into one level interrupt with a
+  pending latch that the host acknowledges, as for the S2MPG12. The
+  interrupt is optional: without it the PMIC still supplies its rails, but
+  none of its events, the RTC alarm among them, reach the host.
+
 properties:
   compatible:
     const: samsung,s2mpg14-pmic
 
+  interrupts:
+    maxItems: 1
+
+  google,vgpio2ap-sysreg:
+    $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/phandle
+    description:
+      Phandle to the VGPIO2AP system registers, which latch the PMIC's
+      in-band interrupt.
+
+  wakeup-source: true
+
   regulators:
     type: object
     $ref: /schemas/regulator/samsung,s2mpg14-regulator.yaml
@@ -26,12 +43,22 @@ required:
   - compatible
   - regulators
 
+dependencies:
+  interrupts: [ 'google,vgpio2ap-sysreg' ]
+  wakeup-source: [ interrupts ]
+
 additionalProperties: false
 
 examples:
   - |
+    #include <dt-bindings/interrupt-controller/arm-gic.h>
+    #include <dt-bindings/interrupt-controller/irq.h>
+
     pmic-1 {
         compatible = "samsung,s2mpg14-pmic";
+        interrupts = <GIC_SPI 74 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
+        google,vgpio2ap-sysreg = <&sysreg_vgpio2ap>;
+        wakeup-source;
 
         regulators {
             ldo4m {
